From: PARP LZX <lzx-note@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mm: apply prediction bins to non-root memcg subtree reclaim

The original reclaim-bin hook only ordered root MGLRU reclaim.  A bounded
application collection normally reaches its parent memory.max and takes the
non-root memcg iterator path, which previously ignored application priors.

When APPLY, the bin switch, and the target policy cgroup are all enabled,
walk descendants in score-bin order and stop when the reclaim goal is met.
Native iterator behavior remains unchanged when the independent switch is
off.  Export pass/selection/skip counters for runtime proof.  lzx-note

